[Audio:start-up-tune:Start-up Tune]
Played by #R$AFBC each time a new game is started.
The music data is at #R$D833.

#AUDIO0(start-up-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(StartUpTune))

[Audio:main-tune:Main Tune]
Played by #R$BB91 while the menu is shown, until a key is pressed.
The music data is at #R$D7CF.

#AUDIO0(main-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(MainTune))

[Audio:collected-tune:Collected Tune]
Played by #R$D0F1 when the helper has collected an object.
The music data is at #R$D847.

#AUDIO0(collected-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(CollectedTune))

[Audio:game-over-tune:Game Over Tune]
Played by #R$C34A when the game is over.
The music data is at #R$D853.

#AUDIO0(game-over-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameOverTune))

[Audio:game-complete-tune:Game Complete Tune]
Played by #R$C320 when all of the stones have been put on the pentagram.
The music data is at #R$D86F.

#AUDIO0(game-complete-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameCompleteTune))

[Audio:unused-tune:Unused Tune]
Never played.
The music data is at #R$D824.

#AUDIO0(unused-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(UnusedTune))

[Audio:jump-sound:Jump Sound]
Played by #R$C588 when the player jumps.
Sixteen single cycles of a tone whose pitch jumps about.

#AUDIO0(jump-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(JumpSound))

[Audio:footstep-sound:Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$C5AE when the player walks, on every fourth step.
The two pitches that the steps alternate between, with four frames between them.

#AUDIO0(footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FootstepSound))

[Audio:shot-sound:Shot Sound]
Played by #R$C1B5 when the player fires a projectile.
Thirty-two single cycles of a tone whose pitch changes.

#AUDIO0(shot-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ShotSound))

[Audio:explosion:Explosion]
Played by #R$C114 for each frame of an explosion.
Each frame has four single cycles of tones with pitches taken from the ROM, so
it is different each time. The seven frames of an explosion, one after the
other.

#AUDIO0(explosion.wav)(#INCLUDE(Explosion))

[Audio:pause-sound:Pause Sound]
Played by #R$B4EB and #R$B50F when the game is paused and when it carries on.
A click, which is a tone that gets a little lower each time that it is made.

#AUDIO0(pause-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(PauseSound))

[Audio:new-room-sound:New Room Sound]
Played by #R$B084, one note each frame, for the four frames after a room is
built.
The four notes, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(new-room-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(NewRoomSound))

[Audio:item-sound:Item Sound]
Played by #R$B084, one note each frame, for the five frames after an object is
picked up or dropped.
The five notes, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(item-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ItemSound))

[Audio:moving-sound:Moving Sound]
Never played, as #R$D56C is not called.
The sixteen pitches of #R$D587, one for each frame.

#AUDIO0(moving-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(MovingSound))

[Audio:object-sound:Object Sound]
Never played, as #R$D665 is not called.
The eight pitches that come from the object types #N$00 to #N$07.

#AUDIO0(object-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ObjectSound))

[Audio:stored-sound:Stored Sound]
Never played, as #R$D673 is not called.
A tone of eight cycles with the pitch #N$FF.

#AUDIO0(stored-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(StoredSound))
